Package: envelopelite
Title: Mortality Envelope by Draw and Linkage of Demographic Estimates
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("TODO", "PLACEHOLDER", email = "todo@example.invalid",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = "TODO placeholder: names, e-mail and ORCID are set by the repository owner before any release")
Description: A thin linkage package: all-cause deaths (the mortality envelope) as
    registered deaths divided by completeness draw by draw, death rates
    paired with population draws, scaling of areas to their total with the
    mismatch reported, and a data contract for packages that estimate causes
    of death, following the conventions of the Global Burden of Disease
    (GBD) study. It is not a life-table engine: its life-table formulas are
    cross-checked against the 'MortalityLaws' package. Development version:
    the shared infrastructure (draws container, per-cell seeds, age groups,
    simulated country with planted truth) is implemented; the linkage
    functions are documented skeletons. This package is an independent
    implementation. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by
    the Institute for Health Metrics and Evaluation (IHME), and it does not
    contain IHME code or data.
